[Music]  welcome back to las vegas now as we  continue to stay home  most of us to stay safe during the  pandemic  you might find yourself repeating  certain recipes and maybe even getting  tired of them  well chef chris with smith's food and  drug is here to help  with a brand new recipe that's sure to  spice up your next meal  and hello everybody i'm chef jeff from  smith's okay it's that time of year  where maybe your  favorite football team is playing or  basketball or maybe it's tuesday  taco we're gonna make some queso because  everybody loves queso and it's super  easy  let's get right to it okay so this is a  creamy cheese okay so but it also has  poblano peppers in it now poblano  peppers are these guys here and their  skin is kind of  it's not very appetizing and so what we  do is we char and get it off there let  me just show you how  we do that so if you've got a gas burner  that's perfect because you just put it  right on that flame  and then it starts to char the skin if  you don't have a gas burner  then you put it right in the broiler  just put it like right underneath your  broiler  and then just let it char that way and  you have to flip it over a few times but  either way  once you get it charred then you put it  in a plastic or in a bowl with cover  with plastic wrap  and let it steam for about 10 minutes  and once you do that  then you're left with this beautiful  charred pepper and then you peel it just  super easily and it comes right off  and you chop it and that's our poblano  pepper we're going to put that in here  in a second  okay the next part of this recipe is the  chorizo  let me get this over here so chorizo you  find  in the back of your local marketplace  next to all the mexican cheeses and  things like that  it's just a delicious sausage got a  bunch of spices in it  what i've done is i've browned some i've  got it all browned and ready to go here  crumbled it  i've taken it out and into that same pan  i'm going to go a little bit of oil  after i've taken the sausage out and i'm  going to do those poblano peppers that i  chopped earlier throw those in  and then next goes some onions some  jalapenos because i like it spicy you  could use serrano peppers they're spicy  as well  and then some garlic because we have to  do garlic and just give those a stir  and let them go for three or four  minutes until the onions are translucent  once you've got to that point i have  right here we're going to throw in our  heavy cream  get that in there like so and give it a  stir and once your heavy cream comes to  a  boil or not even a boil more like a  simmer that's when you're going to add  the cheese and so we'll pretend that  that's happening  right here in this pan so we'll add our  cheddar  and then i've got monterey jack and then  i've got  mozzarella and then you just stir that  in and just becomes the super melty  gooey thing and i have one that's  finished right here all  gooey and delicious you see that perfect  and then what you do next is really  simple you just throw some of that cake  or that  sausage back in there not all of it  because i want to save some of it  and then we're going to give it a stir  and our queso is ready to be served  now what you do i would recommend if you  have one of those mini crock pots or  something like that  and hold it warm that way otherwise just  throw it in a  bowl like this it's looking gooey and  awesome  and then what i do after that is just  top it with some extra  chorizo your guests will love it it's  super simple  super flavorful of course you can find  all these ingredients at your local  smiths  thank you so much for watching thank you  for shopping and we will see you guys  all next time bye-bye  to get this recipe and more information  you can visit smithfoodondrug.com  lindsay

